error: `state:hover` is not one of the states a view may set

       note: the states a view may set are `checked`, `disabled`, `indeterminate`, `invalid`, `open`, `placeholder_shown`, `read_only`, `required`
       help: an author-defined state is written `custom_state:hover=…`, and matches `:state(hover)` in CSS
       note: `hover` is computed by the input system from what the pointer and the keyboard did, so a view cannot assert it
  --> tests/ui/state_not_assertable.rs:15:33
